(ORIOLE REPO | COLLATERAL SCHEDULE OR-6 | 2026-10-01) Tj
T*
(All entities and trades in this schedule are fictional. Currency amounts are in thousands) Tj
T*
(of CNY unless stated otherwise. Exposure means cash principal plus accrued repo interest.) Tj
T*
(Collateral value is the clean market value after the applicable haircut; it is not the) Tj
T*
(security's face value.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(HAIRCUT SCHEDULE) Tj
T*
(Sovereign bonds with remaining maturity up to 1 year: 2%.) Tj
T*
(Sovereign bonds with remaining maturity above 1 year: 4%.) Tj
T*
(Approved corporate bonds: 9%.) Tj
T*
(A corporate issue on the watch list receives an additional 6 percentage points. A missing) Tj
T*
(quote makes that issue ineligible, rather than assigning a zero haircut. The watch-list) Tj
T*
(add-on never applies to sovereign bonds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(VALUATION AND ROUNDING) Tj
T*
(Each issue is valued separately: clean market value multiplied by one minus its total) Tj
T*
(haircut. Sum the issue values without intermediate rounding, then round the total down to) Tj
T*
(the nearest 1 thousand. Accrued bond coupon is excluded. Exposure, in contrast, includes) Tj
T*
(accrued repo interest. The two kinds of accrued amounts must not be interchanged.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(MARKET RECORDS) Tj
T*
(The valuation analyst stores the quote time and source with the issue code. A dealer's) Tj
T*
(indicative email may explain a price change, but is not a substitute for the approved) Tj
T*
(closing quote. A stale quote is treated under the missing-quote rule if it is outside the) Tj
T*
(permitted feed window. Custody receipts describe location and ownership; they do not) Tj
T*
(establish a market price. Reconciliation staff keep the exposure file separate from the) Tj
T*
(collateral file so that a coupon receipt cannot accidentally reduce repo principal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
